# Look-Ahead Bias

A value used for a **decision or feature** at time `t` must depend only on information available **at or before** `t`.

Forward-looking values are allowed **only** as isolated **labels / prediction targets** for training and evaluation — never as features, signals, or inputs to rolling stats at the same row.

## Decision timeline — default daily / bar sleeves (close `t` → open `t+1`)

Align every row to one decision timestamp `t` (bar close). Matches [backtest-integrity](.cursor/rules/backtest-integrity.mdc). This is the **default** for new daily work (including S2 and S3):

| Role | Timestamp | Meaning |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Features & signal | close of `t` | Known at or before close `t` |
| Decision | after close `t` | Enter / exit choice |
| Orders | just before open `t+1` | Queued for the open |
| Fill | open of `t+1` | Next bar’s OHLCV open (no-auction venues) |
| PnL / stops | from open `t+1` onward | Path-check high/low after entry |
| Label (train/eval only) | after fill | Outcome from the fill onward (never a feature on row `t`) |

Row `t` answers: *given everything known at close `t`, what should we trade at the next open?*

**Same-bar close-fill** (decide and fill at close `t`) is **opt-in only** when the sleeve documents that convention and the close is actually executable. Do not use it as the silent default for daily FX / equity / futures research.

## Decision timeline — S1 equities GBM only (trade-date panel)

| Role | Timestamp | Meaning |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Info cutoff | close of `feature_date` | Last completed bar before trade |
| Overnight alt data | after that close, before open `date` | Allowed if it references `feature_date` or earlier (e.g. FINRA same-day file at 18:00 ET) |
| Decision | pre-open `date` | Scores / ranks |
| Fill | open `date` | Entry |
| Label | `Open_{date+h} / Open_date - 1` | Exit at open `date+h` (panel columns `fwd_ret_{h}`) |

Applies to the S1 equities sleeve only (`01_data/data_files/s1_equities/*`, `02_research/notebooks/s1_equities/factor_tests/*`, S1 pooled GBM). Alphalens on S1 pivots `open` with **no** price-frame `shift(-1)`. Same economic lag as close→next-open; different panel indexing.

## Decision timeline — S2 cointegration (signal close `t` → fill open `t+1`)

| Role | Timestamp | Meaning |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Features & signal | close of `t` | `close_y` / `close_x` (and derived β, spread, z, ADF, half-life) |
| Optional alt data | after close `t`, before open `t+1` | Allowed if knowable in that window |
| Decision | after close `t` | Enter / exit choice |
| Orders | just before open `t+1` | Queued for the open |
| Fill | open of `t+1` | Both legs (crypto: next-bar OHLCV open) |
| PnL / HL stops | from open `t+1` onward | Path-check high/low after entry |

Applies to S2 (`01_data/data_files/s2_coint/*`, `02_research/s2_coint/*`, `05_strategies/s2_coint/*`, `04_backtest/s2_coint/*`) at every bar size (1D / 4H / 1H). **Not** S1 trade-date indexing; **not** same-bar close-fill.

## Decision timeline — S3 FX trend (signal close `t` → fill open `t+1`)

| Role | Timestamp | Meaning |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Features & signal | close of `t` | TSMOM / Donchian / gates on the pre-registered daily boundary |
| Optional alt / macro | after close `t`, before open `t+1` | Allowed if knowable then (e.g. rates for carry tilt) |
| Decision | after close `t` | Enter / exit / size |
| Orders | just before open `t+1` | Queued for the open |
| Fill | open of `t+1` | Next tradable open after the defined close |
| PnL / stops | from open `t+1` onward | After fill |

Applies to S3 (`01_data/data_files/s3_fx_trend/*`, `02_research/s3_fx_trend/*`, `05_strategies/s3_fx_trend/*`, future `04_backtest/s3_fx_trend/*`). Pre-register the FX **day boundary** (recommend 17:00 America/New_York, or freeze broker candle TZ). **Not** S1 trade-date indexing; **not** same-bar close-fill.

## Rules

- Lag all rolling stats one bar when the current bar's close/high/low should not be known yet: `.shift(1)` after rolling/ewm, or compute on `t-1` data explicitly. **Exception — S2 / S3 (and the default close→next-open contract):** a close-`t` decision may use close `t` in the signal; the lag is the **fill** at open `t+1`, not an extra `.shift(1)` on features.
- **Never** use `shift(-n)`, `lead`, `bfill`, or forward-looking joins to build **features, signals, or cross-row derived inputs**.
- **Labels / targets only:** `shift(-n)` on price or forward returns is allowed in dedicated target columns (e.g. `open.shift(-h) / open - 1` for S1 `fwd_ret_h`). Keep targets in separate columns; never feed them into feature engineering on the same row.
- Merge auxiliary data with `merge_asof(..., direction='backward')` (or equivalent), never forward-fill from the future. On the S1 trade-date panel, merge alt data on `feature_date` (not trade `date`) so same-morning filings cannot leak.
- Cross-sectional ranks/z-scores at `t` use only the cross-section available at `t` (no full-sample mean/std).
- ML: fit preprocessors, selectors, and models on train only; `transform` val/test. No `fit` on full history. Drop or exclude label columns before `predict` at inference.
- Backtest loop: update portfolio state **after** the fill bar, not using that bar's outcome to decide the same bar.

## Examples

```python
# BAD (optimistic same-bar close fill when you cannot trade that close)
signal = (close > close.rolling(20).mean())
# fill at close t  # only if the sleeve explicitly opts into close-fill

# GOOD (default / S2 / S3) — close t in the signal; fill at next open
signal_t = (close > close.rolling(20).mean())  # known at close t
# fill at open of t+1; do not store next open on the signal row as a feature

# BAD — forward return used as a feature (peeking)
df["fwd_ret"] = close.pct_change(5).shift(-5)
df["feature"] = df["fwd_ret"].rolling(10).mean()

# GOOD — label forward-looking; features use only past / close-t info per contract
df["label"] = close.shift(-1) / close - 1  # evaluation only
df["feature"] = close.pct_change().rolling(10).mean()  # S2/S3: ok at close t

# GOOD (S1 trade-date panel) — open-to-open labels; hlcv already lagged to feature_date
df["fwd_ret_5"] = open.groupby(ticker).shift(-5) / open - 1
# Alphalens: pivot values="open" (no shift)

# GOOD — model trained on target, infers from features only
X = df[["feature"]]                               # no target/label columns
y = df["target"]
# at inference: signal = model.predict(X)  →  order for open t+1 under default/S2/S3
```
